Adam Lawson wrote:
> What cool things can an arch-lich do as a pet? I've had with polymorph 
> traps and luck a lurker-above, a minotaur, and a lot of useless weak 
> pets. I've never had a lich before, much less an arch-lich.

Lich make risky pets in general. They don't eat, which means you get all 
of the corpses, but they also won't gain tameness (without you casting 
"charm" on it) so if you do anything that lowers tameness (like hit a 
levelport trap), eventually it'll go feral and you'll have to deal with it.

Most of what makes lichs powerful foes is their offensive spells, and 
pets won't use them unless confused/conflicted. So it sort of comes down 
to a semi-good pet that can go feral to produce a very dangerous enemy.

